; Looping in lambda always takes the form of repeated functional application.
; We define loops recursively
gauss → (λ i x.
if == i 0
then x 
else
gauss (- i 1) (+ x i)
)
(gauss 100 0)
; gauss aurafarming his teacher

; Let's consider the same program but for n = 3
; Our rule states that gauss(0,x) = x and gauss(a,x) = gauss(a-1,x+a)
; gauss(3,0) = gauss(3-1,3) = gauss(2-1,3+2) = gauss(0,3 + 2 + 1)
; = 6
; In Lambda, our function arugments are our state variables.
